# OPTIONAL testnet2 aggregator (SGW) key. Leave empty (default) and the bot
# provisions its OWN per-wallet free-plan key on first boot — get-or-create by
# the wallet's index-0 identity, gateway URL comes from the SDK's per-network
# config (NETWORKS[network].aggregatorUrl) — and saves it to
# BOT_DATA_DIR/aggregator-key.json, so each bot has its own rate-limit instead
# of sharing one static key's limit with every other example wallet. Reused
# on every later boot (no re-provisioning). Set this to force a specific key
# instead (e.g. a shared/paid one) — this always wins over a saved key.
AGGREGATOR_API_KEY=
# Example public, non-secret testnet2 key (shared rate limit — prefer leaving
# AGGREGATOR_API_KEY empty above so this bot gets its own):
# AGGREGATOR_API_KEY=sk_ddc3cfcc001e4a28ac3fad7407f99590
# The bot's own wallet. Leave BOT_MNEMONIC empty on first run to auto-generate
# (the bot prints the generated mnemonic — save it). Set it to persist identity.
BOT_MNEMONIC=
# Local file storage for the bot's KEYS + identity state. Token custody is NOT
# local any more (sphere-sdk 0.14 deleted own-storage custody) — tokens live in
# the wallet-api inventory keyed by WALLET_API_URL below.
BOT_DATA_DIR=./.bot-data
# REQUIRED. The wallet-api instance that holds this bot's token inventory and
# mailbox. Sphere.init throws INVALID_CONFIG without it — money does not move
# without wallet-api custody.
# Known endpoints:  prod = https://wallet-api.unicity.network
#                   staging = https://wallet-api.staging.unicity.network
WALLET_API_URL=https://wallet-api.unicity.network
# OPTIONAL stable device label for the wallet-api refresh token. Omit it and
# every run performs a fresh challenge sign-in.
BOT_DEVICE_ID=
